    "turn_text": "pathetic. You've got to ask yourself this, Patrick, how did we get here? How is it that so many people know about Lady Gaga and Miley Cyrus's rear-end? How is it that so many people in this country know about the television show Breaking Bad? How is it that anybody knows about all these pop culture issues but don't know much about politics? We got there somehow. And I think what Ted Cruz did was he started the process of getting people to get back engaged in government. A hundred years ago, everybody in this country wanted to make sure that those in Washington knew who ran the joint. It's us, the people. We can do that again. We just have to stick to our guns and make sure that we teach our kids right, make sure the next generation knows the structure of government and make sure that they understand Freedom and liberty comes at a cost and the cost is A, you get engaged and B, you might actually have to go up and pick up arms and go overseas and fight for what we believe in. At the end of the day, we can fix this. I'm not a defeatist like you are. I'm somebody who believes that we can bring it back around, but I appreciate it. I'm not somebody who ever throws my hands up and says, forget it, we can't do anything. I'm not that guy. I'm not. I'm the guy that says, we're going to put you back in your place. And you're going to serve at our whim and at our leisure or our pleasure. And if you don't do it the way that we want you to do it, we're going to find somebody who will. We've gotten lulled into believing that because somebody is attractive to us through pop culture, like Barack Obama, that we have to just shut up and take anything he wants to dole out. We don't. We don't. We have the right to put our feet down and say, you're going to listen to us now. you're going to stop sweat you know drifting off the path of freedom and liberty you're going to stop drifting away from what this country was founded on and you're going to do what we want all you're not going to well then we're never going to do it to give you that that sense of power again we're going to take it back because it's really ours What right now we've got a bunch of drones walking around taking selfies and worrying about who sounded better, Adam Lambert or the guy from, what's the fun, singing with Queen. We're more interested in that than the legislative process and that's something historic happened in Washington this week. I aim to change that. Listen, you can like Queen's music and you can like Miley Cyrus and you can like the Kardashians as long as that second or third or fifth down the line. The first thing you should be worried about when it comes to our society is who's running it. And are they doing it the way that you would want them to do it? That's what you've got to answer for yourself. All right, 1-800-500-170-80, 1-800-500-170-80, facebook.com slash the weekend. Joe talk show, if you want to get ahold of me, jotalkshow.com. Go like my stuff too. Keep it here on the weekend.",
