    "turn_text": "i mean my hope was by spending an extended period of time focusing the debate on obama care on how this this Law is not working, how it's the biggest job killer in the country, how millions of Americans are suffering under it. They're losing their jobs. They can't find jobs. They're being forced into part-time work, working 29 hours a week. They're facing skyrocketing health insurance premiums, or they're losing their health insurance, or being threatened with losing their health insurance. It isn't working. And there is nothing like a filibuster, an extended, concentrated, focused discussion and debate. to impact and focus the national conversation and that was certainly my hope is that it would have a positive effect and it would serve as an outlet for the millions of americans across this country who quite rightly feel they don't have a voice in washington they're not being listened to and i was trying to do my best to use What little ability I have to speak on their behalf, and I hope it had some positive effect in that",
