    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 66259,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66259.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Joe, you're absolutely right. The people who are the biggest losers under Obamacare. are the most vulnerable among us their young people are coming out of school unable to find a job uh... their single moms who you know maybe working waiting tables and suddenly find find their hours forcibly reduced to twenty nine hours a week you can't feed your kids on twenty nine hours a week their Hispanics and african-americans who are struggling to climb the economic ladder and and who may find suddenly they can't get a job there in part-time work or their health insurance premiums are skyrocketing or their seniors or people's with disabilities they're being told your health insurance is being dropped because of obama care and and and one of the things we try to do during the filibuster spent a great deal of the time just reading stories of of americans all across our nation who are facing this right now who are losing their health insurance because of obama care and and to say this thing isn't working and it is hurting those who are struggling the most And we've got to pull up and stop this train wreck, this nightmare of legislation.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_06",
