    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "It's Senator Ted Cruz, the junior senator from the great state of Texas. You at one point during the filibuster said it shouldn't be one or two or three or four senators in this chamber. It should be a 100. Both sides of the aisle should have gone. There should have witnessed this historic event. and should have at least made note of what it was that you guys were doing that was so different from what the old school was doing. The next day after a good night's sleep and I think after dinner with Harry Reid, John McCain put down his iPhone and his poker game long enough to come out and say, I respect Ted Cruz, he's a great guy, but how dare he say, and he, I guess one of his staffers pulled a phrase or a sentence out of 21 hours plus and decided to tell you here, how dare you compare something to World War II? Did they just, generally speaking, John McCain aside, generally speaking, those who didn't get what you were doing, they really just didn't get what you were doing, or Ted, do you think they got it and just disagreed with it?",
