    "turn_text": "well what we'll tell the thing is that we don't care about the little fiefdoms that everybody's built in the senator in the house right what we care is that you're doing the bidding of the people that sent you there and and i've got to tell you before we were on a work run at a time i am overtly proud of you I did a monologue in a rant after you got done speaking the other day. I sent it to you and I sent it to Catherine in your office. Hopefully, when you're done doing the massive media tour that I'm sure you're doing, you'll have time to listen to it because it really hit me in a way that I want to make sure you hear with your ears. So, I mean, I'm 100% in support of what you did. I talked to Cornyn earlier today, and the reason I bring up the statement that you made that all 100 senators should be here, I mentioned that to him. And I said, why weren't you there? Why not walk in even but for a few minutes to say he's on my team. He's from my state. He's doing something that I approve of. And his comment said, and he said specifically this, that was Ted's thing. I didn't want to take away from the limelight that he was getting. Do you buy that or did he stay away because he didn't want to be lumped in with you?",
