    "turn_idx": 62,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm not sure what the House is going to do, and I certainly don't want to try to dictate to them what they should do. What I've publicly said in terms of my own vote is that I'm not going to vote for any continuing resolution that funds Obamacare. And I'll say, listen, last week, The House stood strong, they passed a strong bill defunding Obamacare, they listened to the American people, and I've got a great deal of hope and optimism, they'll continue to stand strong. And when they pass a bill that goes directly to mitigating the harms from Obamacare for the American people, then it's time for senate republicans to unify to stand together we shouldn't be throwing rocks at each other we should be standing arm in arm with the house republicans alongside the american people and i'll mention just this is just as a final point in the last several weeks we've seen nearly one point nine million people sign the national petition at don't find it dot com that has played a huge part in causing the house to do the right thing in framing the debate and so everyone listening if you agree that we need to ticket the house to continue to have leadership and the senate to come together and support the house and i would encourage you go to don't find a dot com sign the national petition speak out to your representatives and get your friends and family to do the same",
